n guidance for each.\n\nOut of scope: any code, operator, or default-configuration change, and serverless-mode disconnected support.\n\nThe source material exists in field enablement docs; this epic is authoring and technical review work, not investigation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode is published in the product documentation, covering prerequisites, operator configuration (including which operators to skip), and validation steps.\n- The guide contains a complete image-mirroring reference: the list of required images and a procedure showing how to derive the digest list per release.\n- The guide contains a troubleshooting section covering image pull errors, missing runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration.\n- The guide's technical claims are accuracy-validated against the platform architecture context for KServe — in particular that raw deployment mode (plain Deployments/Services, no mesh dependency) is the recommended path for disconnected environments, that Service Mesh / Serverless operators are serverless-mode-only dependencies, and that Serving Runtimes provide model execution — and the guide is technically reviewed by the engineering owners of the KServe component before publication.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)**: Disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode in product documentation (prerequisites, operator configuration, validation steps) — fully covered by this epic.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Complete image-mirroring reference (required images and digest-list derivation per release) — fully covered by this epic.\n- **HLR-3 (P2)**: Troubleshooting section for the three most common field-reported failure modes — fully covered by this epic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":21158,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd195944cfd4b299","agent_id":"ac4b8332f2d72ffb