{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f2e66fcb-3e4f-4caf-a817-d8edb0354695","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Decomposition of RHAISTRAT-9004 is complete.\n\n**Triage outcome**: Check 2 (documentation-only) fired. The strategy's own text confirms the capability exists and works, the out-of-scope section excludes all code/operator/config changes, and open questions are explicitly \"None — this is authoring and technical review work.\" Per Step 0, this produced a single `docs-authoring` epic with no DAG and no multi-step decomposition.\n\n**Artifacts written** (all under `/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9004-51pj6f35/artifacts/epic-tasks/`):\n- `RHAISTRAT-9004-E001.md` — single Implementation epic, `implementation_type: docs-authoring`, priority P1 (docs-authoring exception: strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1, consistent with HLR-1/HLR-2 at P1), component `Documentation` (canonical, verbatim from `.context/rhai-components.txt`), team `RHOAI Serving`, no dependencies. All 9 `ai_signals` set; body carries the four required sections with the content outline inside Scope and an accuracy-validation AC against the KServe architecture context file.\n- `RHAISTRAT-9004-E001-ai-signals.md` — signal rationale table (Implementation 9-signal set; `human_process_gates: -1` for the mandatory docs technical review, rest favorable).\n- `RHAISTRAT-9004-decomposition.md` — summary with triage rationale, single-node DAG, full HLR traceability (HLR-1/2/3 all covered by E001), and health warnings.\n\n**Key notes for the caller**:\n- Health warnings logged: the strategy lacks the structured sections (Affected Components change/owner columns, Impacted Teams, dependencies table, Given/When/Then ACs, NFRs), and team attribution was inferred as RHOAI Serving from the KServe architecture context (`kserve.md` lists it as owning team) — flag for reviewer confirmation in case a separate docs team owns autho