{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-958da7ac16ddd417","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9004-E001\n3\ttitle: Disconnected environment install guide for KServe raw deployment mode\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9004\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Disconnected environment install guide for KServe raw deployment mode\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers a disconnected-environment (air-gapped) installation guide for KServe raw deployment mode as published product documentation. The capability itself already exists and works — no code, operator, or default-configuration changes are in scope. The deliverable converts existing field enablement material and private field-team knowledge into a customer-facing guide covering prerequisites, operator configuration, image mirroring, install validation, and troubleshooting for raw deployment mode on disconnected clusters.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\tAuthor and publish a new documentation topic covering disconnected installs of KServe raw deployment mode, with the following content outline:\n38\t\n39\t- **Prerequisites**: hardware/cluster requirements and any constraints specific to disconnected environments for raw deployment mode.\n40\t- **Operator configuration**: which operators are required for raw deployment mode, and explicitly which operators to skip (the serverless-mode-only ones, e.g. Service Mesh / Serverless operators that raw deployment mode does not need).\n41\t- **Image mirroring reference**: the complete list of required images to mirror for a raw deployment mode install, plus the procedure for deriving the image digest list per release.\n42\t- **Validation steps**: how to verify a successful air-gapped install of KServe raw deployment mode.\n43\t- **Troubleshooting**: the three most common field-reported failure modes — image pull errors, missing runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration — with diagnosis and remediation guidance for each.\n44\t\n45\tOut of scope: any code, operator, or default-configuration change, and serverless-mode disconnected support.\n46\t\n47\tThe source material exists in field enablement docs; this epic is authoring and technical review work, not investigation.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- A disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode is published in the product documentation, covering prerequisites, operator configuration (including which operators to skip), and validation steps.\n52\t- The guide contains a complete image-mirroring reference: the list of required images and a procedure showing how to derive the digest list per release.\n53\t- The guide contains a troubleshooting section covering image pull errors, missing runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration.\n54\t- The guide's technical claims are accuracy-validated against the platform architecture context for KServe — in particular that raw deployment mode (plain Deployments/Services, no mesh dependency) is the recommended path for disconnected environments, that Service Mesh / Serverless operators are serverless-mode-only dependencies, and that Serving Runtimes provide model execution — and the guide is technically reviewed by the engineering owners of the KServe component before publication.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- **HLR-1 (P1)**: Disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode in product documentation (prerequisites, operator configuration, validation steps) — fully covered by this epic.\n59\t- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Complete image-mirroring reference (required images and digest-list derivation per release) — fully covered by this epic.\n60\t- **HLR-3 (P2)**: Troubleshooting section for the three most common field-reported failure modes — fully covered by this epic.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f602fe74890be91","agent_id":"a8f2a84b8981ec845","session_id":"50f818fe-63f0-4918-bd96-bec61faaccd7","uuid":"5ef6ee9d-822a-42f8-8194-84cd417cf451","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:29:37.640Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-958da7ac16ddd417","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9004 decomposition"}
